From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:36:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: bound the link assessments of a display that is off

A display whose FRL caps were restored from its last link training and
that has no head is assessed again on every EDID read, which every
connector probe does, so also every hotplug event of any other display
and every resume. Each assessment is a link training under nvkms_lock,
during which flips and vblank callbacks of all heads wait. The probe
resets frlLinkFailures before it assesses, so the limit on reported
failures that drops the restored caps is never reached on this path: a
sink that stays in standby with a readable EDID, like a TV that is
switched off but connected, is trained against on every probe for as
long as it stays that way.

Count these assessments in a counter of their own and stop after three.
It starts over when the caps are restored anew and when the sink itself
is hotplugged, so a sink that wakes up later still gets its tries. After
that, the restored caps stay until a hotplug of the sink or a modeset
trains the link, which is what a display in use gets already.

How long an assessment against a sink in standby takes was not measured.

Fixes: 0900425f654d ("nvkms: keep the HDMI FRL caps of a sink that isn't ready for link training")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hdmi.h  |  3 +++
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h |  5 +++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c       | 11 ++++++++++-
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c      |  1 +
 4 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hdmi.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hdmi.h
index 61a5f636..b05da260 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hdmi.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hdmi.h
@@ -71,6 +71,9 @@ void nvTeardownHdmiLibrary(NVDevEvoRec *pDevEvo);
 
 NvBool nvHdmiFrlAssessLink(NVDpyEvoPtr pDpyEvo);
 NvBool nvHdmiFrlRestoreTrainedCaps(NVDpyEvoPtr pDpyEvo);
+
+/* Link assessments of a display that is off while its FRL caps are restored. */
+#define MAX_RESTORED_FRL_ASSESSMENTS 3
 NvBool nvHdmiDpySupportsFrl(const NVDpyEvoRec *pDpyEvo);
 NvBool nvHdmiScdcWantsForceFrl(const NVDpyEvoRec *pDpyEvo);
 void nvHdmiRefreshScdcSrcTestConfig(NVDpyEvoPtr pDpyEvo);
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
index 51a4ad7e..cde44f95 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
@@ -2456,6 +2456,11 @@ typedef struct _NVDpyEvoRec {
         /* srcCaps and sinkCaps came from lastTrainedFrl, not an assessment. */
         NvBool frlCapsRestored                 : 1;
         NvU8 frlLinkFailures;
+        /*
+         * Link assessments of a display that is off while its caps are
+         * restored, since the caps were restored or the sink was hotplugged.
+         */
+        NvU8 frlRestoredAssessments;
 
         /*
          * The caps of the last link training that succeeded, and the EDID they
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c
index 704c4438..edb1aef0 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c
@@ -776,16 +776,25 @@ static void ReadAndApplyEdidEvo(
              * Note that this also takes care of HDMI FRL link re-assessment
              * on hotplugs.
              */
+            pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlRestoredAssessments = 0;
             nvDpyProbeMaxPixelClock(pDpyEvo);
         } else if (nvDpyIsHdmiEvo(pDpyEvo) &&
             nvHdmiDpySupportsFrl(pDpyEvo) &&
             pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlCapsRestored &&
-            (pDpyEvo->apiHead == NV_INVALID_HEAD)) {
+            (pDpyEvo->apiHead == NV_INVALID_HEAD) &&
+            (pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlRestoredAssessments <
+             MAX_RESTORED_FRL_ASSESSMENTS)) {
             /*
              * The FRL caps are left from an earlier link training because the
              * link couldn't be assessed. Try again while the display is off;
              * for a display in use, its next modeset's link training decides.
+             *
+             * Each try is a link training under nvkms_lock and the probe
+             * resets frlLinkFailures, so bound the tries in a counter of
+             * their own. Once they are used up, the restored caps stay until
+             * the sink is hotplugged or a modeset trains the link.
              */
+            pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlRestoredAssessments++;
             nvDpyProbeMaxPixelClock(pDpyEvo);
         } else if (nvDpyIsHdmiEvo(pDpyEvo) &&
             nvHdmiDpySupportsFrl(pDpyEvo) &&
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c
index c4b9437c..bddb26d2 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c
@@ -2388,6 +2388,7 @@ NvBool nvHdmiFrlRestoreTrainedCaps(NVDpyEvoPtr pDpyEvo)
     pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlCapsRestored = TRUE;
 
     if (!wasRestored) {
+        pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlRestoredAssessments = 0;
         nvEvoLogDisp(pDpyEvo->pDispEvo, EVO_LOG_WARN,
                      "HDMI FRL link assessment failed, "
                      "keeping the caps of the last link training.");
